### 6. Compute Sizing for 5 TB+ Workloads

| Workload | Compute Type | Size | Why |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Incremental bronze ingestion (50 GB/day) | Job Cluster (Photon) | Medium | Short-lived, moderate data volume |
| Silver pre-join (5 TB initial, 50 GB/day incremental) | Job Cluster (Photon) | Large | Heavy join on first run; Medium after |
| Gold MERGE (CDF-based, \~500 MB changes) | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) | Small | Small data volume, instant start |
| Gold MV refresh | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) | Medium | Auto-scales for multiple MVs |
| Window function recompute (90 days = \~500 GB) | Job Cluster (Photon) | Large | Heavy sort + shuffle |
| Dashboard serving (100 concurrent users) | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) | Medium, max clusters = 5 | Auto-scales horizontally |
| Monthly full recompute (backfill) | Job Cluster (Photon) | X-Large + spot workers | One-off, cost-optimize with spot |
| OPTIMIZE + VACUUM (5 TB table) | SQL Warehouse (Serverless) | Medium | I/O intensive, benefits from Photon |

**Spot instance strategy for batch:**
```
Driver:   On-demand (never lose the driver)
Workers:  80% spot / 20% on-demand
Fallback: If spot preempted, on-demand workers keep the job alive
Savings:  ~60% on worker costs
```

